        <section id="faq" class="faq-section">
          <h2>FAQ</h2>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Does a bigger goal always mean more total tips?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>No — a goal sized past what your room can realistically finish tends to lower total tips, since an obviously-stalled bar discourages further contribution rather than encouraging it.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Should the tip menu and goal ever compete for attention?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>They shouldn't be pushed with equal weight at the same moment. Let one lead at a time — menu items early to warm the room up, the goal once there's a real audience in it.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How often should tip menu prices change?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>Full repricing isn't necessary often, but rotating 1–2 items every few weeks keeps regulars actually reading the menu instead of tuning it out as background decoration.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Does goal/tip-menu structure affect StripScore?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>Indirectly, yes — tips and goal completions are one of the signals StripScore weighs (see what StripScore actually measures in our <a href="/stripscore-cam-rank-explained">full explainer</a>), so a menu/goal structure that actually converts feeds that signal more consistently than one that just sits there. See our <a href="/how-stripscore-works">full breakdown of what builds StripScore →</a></p></div>
          </div>
        </section>

